      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, for two reasons.\n\n1. **The dose is unsafe.** The maximum recommended adult dose of amlodipine is 10 mg once daily. A 50 mg dose is five times that. It could cause severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, shock, and prolonged toxicity, because amlodipine has a long half-life. It may be a typo, for example 5 mg.\n\n2. **You aren't a clinician.** Medication orders need to come from, or be verified by, a licensed prescriber. I can't confirm that this order has been authorized.\n\nI can enter the order once a prescriber confirms the intended dose. For example, the prescriber might confirm amlodipine 5 mg by mouth once daily, or 10 mg if that's what they intend. If a clinician really does intend 50 mg, they should enter it themselves and document why."
      }
